1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,700
A bear stands up on the trail ahead of you, and every instinct in your body screams run.

2
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:09,434
If you listen to that instinct, you lose.

3
00:00:09,484 --> 00:00:18,317
Today, seven animal encounters, and exactly what to do in each one, because the right move is almost never the one your body wants to make.

4
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:21,734
And number one could save your life this very summer.

5
00:00:23,084 --> 00:00:23,858
Number seven.

6
00:00:23,908 --> 00:00:25,095
An aggressive dog.

7
00:00:25,145 --> 00:00:30,454
If a strange dog charges you, do not run, and do not scream.

8
00:00:30,504 --> 00:00:34,988
Running turns you into prey, and dogs are faster than you.

9
00:00:35,038 --> 00:00:39,934
Stand still, turn sideways, and keep your hands up near your chest.

10
00:00:39,984 --> 00:00:44,056
Avoid staring into its eyes, that reads as a challenge.

11
00:00:44,106 --> 00:00:47,766
In dog language, boring things are not worth biting.

12
00:00:47,816 --> 00:00:55,598
If it does attack, feed it your jacket, your bag, anything but your arms, and back away toward safety.

13
00:00:56,948 --> 00:00:57,627
Number six.

14
00:00:57,677 --> 00:00:59,086
A swarm of bees.

15
00:00:59,136 --> 00:01:00,180
Forget the movies.

16
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:07,472
Do not jump into a pond, bees will simply wait above the surface for you to come up for air.

17
00:01:07,522 --> 00:01:12,212
And do not swat, crushed bees release a scent that calls for backup.

18
00:01:12,262 --> 00:01:12,941
Instead, run.

19
00:01:12,991 --> 00:01:16,587
Bees defend their hive, they will not chase you forever.

20
00:01:16,637 --> 00:01:25,338
Run in a straight line, cover your face with your shirt, and get inside a building or a car as fast as you can.

21
00:01:26,688 --> 00:01:27,393
Number five.

22
00:01:27,443 --> 00:01:28,525
A snake bite.

23
00:01:28,575 --> 00:01:29,657
First, the don'ts.

24
00:01:29,707 --> 00:01:40,599
Do not suck out the venom, do not cut the wound, and do not tie a tourniquet, those tricks belong in old western movies, and they make things worse.

25
00:01:40,649 --> 00:01:50,033
Instead, move away from the snake, stay as calm as you can, and keep the bitten limb still, and below the level of your heart.

26
00:01:50,083 --> 00:01:52,297
A racing heart pumps venom faster.

27
00:01:52,347 --> 00:01:57,202
Remove rings and watches before the swelling starts, and get to a hospital.

28
00:01:58,552 --> 00:01:59,265
Number four.

29
00:01:59,315 --> 00:02:01,174
A shark, way too close.

30
00:02:01,224 --> 00:02:06,899
Splashing and paddling away in a panic makes you look exactly like a wounded seal.

31
00:02:06,949 --> 00:02:11,860
Instead, stay vertical in the water, and keep your eyes on the shark.

32
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:15,296
Sharks are ambush hunters, and they hate being watched.

33
00:02:15,346 --> 00:02:21,402
Back up slowly against a reef or a rock, so nothing can approach you from behind.

34
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:27,127
If it comes at you anyway, go for the nose, the gills, and the eyes.

35
00:02:27,177 --> 00:02:28,654
Poke, do not slap.

36
00:02:30,004 --> 00:02:30,709
Number three.

37
00:02:30,759 --> 00:02:31,465
A moose.

38
00:02:31,515 --> 00:02:33,353
And here is the twist.

39
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:36,752
Everything you just learned about not running, forget it.

40
00:02:36,802 --> 00:02:46,571
When a moose pins its ears back and lowers its head, you run, and you put something big between you, a tree, a car, a boulder.

41
00:02:46,621 --> 00:02:51,858
Moose are not predators, they just want you gone, and they rarely chase far.

42
00:02:51,908 --> 00:02:59,034
If one knocks you down, curl into a ball, protect your head, and stay still until it moves away.

43
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:01,177
Number two.

44
00:03:01,227 --> 00:03:02,441
A mountain lion.

45
00:03:02,491 --> 00:03:08,339
With big cats, size is everything, so become the biggest thing on that trail.

46
00:03:08,389 --> 00:03:14,237
Open your jacket wide, raise your arms, and speak in a loud, firm voice.

47
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:22,242
Back away slowly, and never, ever crouch down or turn your back, because that is exactly how prey behaves.

48
00:03:22,292 --> 00:03:26,877
If it keeps coming, throw stones, branches, whatever you can reach.

49
00:03:26,927 --> 00:03:29,826
And if it attacks, fight back hard.

50
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:33,618
People have driven off cougars with their bare hands.

51
00:03:34,968 --> 00:03:36,112
And number one.

52
00:03:36,162 --> 00:03:36,908
A bear.

53
00:03:36,958 --> 00:03:38,102
Do not run.

54
00:03:38,152 --> 00:03:44,073
No human has ever outrun a bear, they can hit thirty five miles per hour.

55
00:03:44,123 --> 00:03:51,238
Instead, stand your ground, speak in a calm, low voice, and back away slowly, sideways if you can.

56
00:03:51,288 --> 00:03:58,004
If a black bear actually attacks, fight back with everything you have, and aim for the face.

57
00:03:58,054 --> 00:04:07,159
If a grizzly knocks you down after a surprise encounter, play dead, flat on your stomach, with your hands locked behind your neck.

58
00:04:07,209 --> 00:04:09,946
And in bear country, carry bear spray.

59
00:04:09,996 --> 00:04:12,334
It works better than anything else.

60
00:04:13,684 --> 00:04:17,032
So here is the pattern behind all seven.

61
00:04:17,082 --> 00:04:23,829
Predators chase whatever runs, so with dogs, big cats, sharks, and bears, you stand your ground.

62
00:04:23,879 --> 00:04:30,201
And with a moose, the one animal that only wants space, you give it space.

63
00:04:30,251 --> 00:04:31,051
Quick recap.

64
00:04:31,101 --> 00:04:32,325
Dog, be boring.

65
00:04:32,375 --> 00:04:34,874
Bees, run in a straight line.

66
00:04:34,924 --> 00:04:38,272
Snake, stay calm and keep the bite low.

67
00:04:38,322 --> 00:04:39,971
Shark, keep eye contact.

68
00:04:40,021 --> 00:04:42,945
Moose, run and hide behind a tree.

69
00:04:42,995 --> 00:04:45,493
Mountain lion, look huge and fight.

70
00:04:45,543 --> 00:04:48,042
Bear, stand your ground, never run.

71
00:04:48,092 --> 00:04:56,113
If this could save your next hike, share it with the friend you hike with, and subscribe for more.

72
00:04:56,163 --> 00:05:00,786
Stay safe, stay curious, and see you in the next one.
